; MiSTer RTG -- mmu.library configuration
;
; Append to ENVARC:MMU-Configuration (then copy to ENV:, or reboot).
; mmu.library reads the file when it initialises, which is before SetPatch
; installs 68040.library, so the regions are tagged before anything builds a
; page table.
;
; WHY THIS IS NEEDED
;
; Every other graphics board in the stock MMU-Configuration is declared with
; a "For <manufacturer> <product>" clause, because AutoConfig gave it a
; ConfigDev and mmu.library can find it by ID.  The MiSTer RTG board has no
; ConfigDev at all: MiSTer.card.asm hardcodes REGISTER_BASE $b80100 and
; MEMORY_BASE $02000000 and never calls FindConfigDev, so expansion.library
; never learns the board exists.  With nothing to tag, mmu.library leaves
; both regions marked Blank -- address space it believes holds nothing --
; and MuScan shows exactly that:
;
;   0x00A80000 - 0x00BBFFFF  Blank WriteThrough          <- the registers
;   0x00BC0000 - 0x00BFFFFF  CacheInhibit I/O space      <- real I/O, tagged
;   0x02000000 - 0x027FFFFF  Imprecise NonSerial Blank   <- the framebuffer
;
; On a CPU without an MMU the hardcoded addresses simply work, which is why
; RTG is fine on the stock TG68K core.  On the 040 the pages are not mapped,
; so every register access faults -- reading the RTG ID at $B8010E gives
; $0000 where the hardware returns $5001 -- and every pixel write goes
; nowhere.  Hence: works before SetPatch, black screen after it.
;
; SYNTAX -- read this before editing, the two forms are not interchangeable
;
; With no ConfigDev there is nothing for a "For" clause to match, so these
; are standalone commands with literal addresses.  The stock file's lines are
; all positional inside a For clause ("For 8512 34 Z3 SetCacheMode {base}
; {size} Valid IOSpace CacheInhibit"); the form documented for standalone use
; with literal addresses is the KEYWORD form, which is what is used below:
;
;     SetCacheMode from <address> size <size> <flags>
;
; If your mmu.library rejects that, the positional equivalent is
;
;     SetCacheMode <address> <size> <flags>
;
; and either way mmu.library reports a parse error at boot rather than
; failing silently, so a wrong guess is visible immediately.
;
; The flags follow the stock file's own convention for a graphics board, and
; the VA2000 entry splits exactly this way: a register block is Valid IOSpace
; CacheInhibit -- cache-inhibited SERIALIZED, so ordering is preserved across
; register writes -- and video memory adds NonSerial Imprecise for fast
; uncached writes.  Note the framebuffer already reads back as Imprecise
; NonSerial above; the only thing changing there is Blank -> Valid IOSpace.
;
; Addresses come from MiSTer.card.asm: REGISTER_BASE $b80100 lives in the 4K
; page fastchip decodes at $B80000-$B80FFF (addr[23:12] == 'hB80, palette
; included), and MEMORY_BASE $02000000 with MEMORY_SIZE $800000.  Both are
; page aligned at the 4K page size MuScan reports.
;
; VERIFY AFTERWARDS with showmmu: $00B80000 should read "CacheInhibit I/O
; space", and the 0x02000000-0x027FFFFF line should lose "Blank".

;MiSTer RTG registers ($B80000-$B80FFF: control block and CLUT)
SetCacheMode from 0x00b80000 size 0x00001000 Valid IOSpace CacheInhibit

;MiSTer RTG framebuffer (MEMORY_BASE, MEMORY_SIZE = 8MB)
SetCacheMode from 0x02000000 size 0x00800000 Valid IOSpace CacheInhibit NonSerial Imprecise
